From c7106724d7dd10ca465cd0d7ab257f8148924665 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:13:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Advent ready (U13): the calendar in order, honest about
 its dates, and findable from Home

James kept the December 1 to 25 family Advent calendar (2026-10-26) and
asked for it fixed: wording, order, findable from home. No new writing.

- Order: the road to Bethlehem (Luke 2:1-5) now comes on December 20,
  before the birth, the shepherds, Mary, and Simeon; it had come on
  December 24, after them. Every day's text is unchanged; only its place
  and label moved.
- Wording: the booklet's cover says Advent begins on the fourth Sunday
  before Christmas (November 27 to December 3) and that the booklet is a
  December 1 to Christmas calendar; the Advent tab names this year's
  Advent Sunday; the "How to Keep Advent" how-to lit its first candle on
  "the first Sunday of December" (December 6 this year) and now says
  "the first Sunday of Advent".
- Findable: from the Sunday a week before Advent Sunday (November 22 in
  2026) through Christmas Day, one line on Home and a card on /family,
  read from the generated year map and the reader's clock, never the
  network. Both link to /family/devotions?season=advent&day=N, which
  opens the Advent tab at tonight's day and marks it.
- Tests: the window, the days, and the copy for every year on the map;
  Luke's story read in order through Christmas Eve; Home, /family, and
  /family/devotions rendered with the clock set.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JuCQ8kZ25i9zRwNgk6bh4e
